<h5>Pages</h5>
<p>Create static pages with title, slug, HTML body, optional <strong>visual layout builder</strong> (Section → Row → Column → Module — including <strong>Carousel</strong>, <strong>Accordion</strong>, <strong>Tabs</strong>, <strong>Icon list</strong>, <strong>Gallery</strong>, <strong>Testimonials</strong>, <strong>Video</strong>, and <strong>Inner row</strong>), optional <strong>block builder</strong> (heading, paragraph, image, columns, CTA, spacer, custom HTML), draft/published status, optional <strong>parent page</strong> (hierarchy + breadcrumbs), and content width override. The page title is used for the browser tab, SEO, menus, and breadcrumbs — it is <strong>not</strong> repeated as an <code>h1</code> inside the public content (put headings in the visual builder instead). <strong>Public render order:</strong> visual layout → block builder → body. Open <strong>Edit via Frontend editor</strong> on an existing page to design the layout on a canvas that looks like the public site. Use <strong>Desktop / Tablet / Mobile</strong> to preview widths, dim modules set to hide on mobile or desktop, and edit Design for that device (tablet CSS applies below 1024px, mobile below 768px; desktop values are the default). Save reusable layouts under <strong>Templates</strong> (shared across pages and posts). On a row, use the <strong>Columns</strong> button or the side panel picker to choose 1–4 columns or common splits. Click <strong>+ Module</strong> (or an empty column, or <strong>+</strong> after a module) to pick a type from the side panel (filter box at the top). Add <strong>Inner row</strong> inside a column to split that column again (one nested row only — Inner row is hidden when you already are inside one). The right-hand designer has <strong>Content</strong> (fields for that module type — heading text and level, captions, button style, and so on; copy, media, links; Text, CTA, and Blurb bodies plus Accordion/Tabs item bodies use a Bold / Italic / list / Link toolbar — scripts and extra tags are stripped on save; headings stay plain; Custom HTML is still for embeds; Accordion items use native expand/collapse on the public page; <strong>Tabs</strong> switch with no extra JavaScript; <strong>Icon list</strong> is emoji/symbol plus text (HTML escaped); <strong>Gallery</strong> is an image grid (2–4 columns); <strong>Testimonials</strong> are quotes with optional photo; Video accepts a YouTube, Vimeo, or HTTPS .mp4/.webm/.ogg URL only; edits update the selected module without rebuilding the whole canvas; carousel slides and accordion/tabs/icon-list add/remove still rebuild), <strong>Design</strong> (fields depend on the module: Heading includes type, Image has no type, Spacer is spacing only; alignment, colors, top/right/bottom/left spacing, spacing presets, theme tokens, allowlisted font / letter spacing / text transform, border, corners, shadow, section background image and overlay, allowlisted shape dividers (wave/tilt/curve/triangle), and a YouTube/Vimeo/HTTPS video background (the canvas shows a placeholder and never loads the iframe); rows can reverse columns on mobile; modules have <strong>Normal / Hover</strong> when the module has color, type, or chrome — hover is the same on every device; <strong>Copy style</strong> / <strong>Paste style</strong> copies appearance only), and <strong>Advanced</strong> (CSS class, visibility, allowlisted sticky and z-index — no absolute/fixed). Color fields include a picker plus hex, or **theme tokens** (Accent / Text / Surface and so on) so the block follows Appearance → Customize. Canvas links do not leave the editor. Unsaved changes warn before leaving the page; dirty layouts also autosave about every 12 seconds. Drag the <strong>⋮⋮</strong> handle to reorder sections, rows, columns, or modules (↑ ↓ still work; nested inner columns and modules use ↑ ↓ only). Select a column for a <strong>1–12 width</strong> slider and <strong>min height</strong>; drag the edge between two columns to split their widths. Open <strong>Layers</strong> for a structure tree (filter box; drag a row to reorder; hover to preview on the canvas; inner columns are not Layers-draggable). Click a heading or text module to type on the canvas. Right-click a block (or use toolbar <strong>Copy</strong> / <strong>Paste</strong> / Ctrl/Cmd+C / V / X). Press <strong>?</strong> for shortcuts. Text align on Design applies to inner wrappers too (Blurb stays centered until you set it). Design colors, spacing, and min height apply live (a stylesheet, not a full canvas rebuild). Switch Desktop / Tablet / Mobile to set per-device spacing and colors (stored in <code>layout_json</code>). Zoom, device preview, and Layers stay for this browser tab. The inspector shows <strong>Section / Row / Col</strong> crumbs so you can jump to a parent. <strong>Undo</strong> and <strong>Redo</strong> are in the toolbar (Ctrl/Cmd+Z and Ctrl/Cmd+Y); Ctrl/Cmd+S saves, Ctrl/Cmd+D duplicates, Alt+arrows nudge order, Escape deselects (again to close Layers), Delete removes (with a confirm). <strong>Revisions:</strong> each save and layout save stores a snapshot (up to 50); restore from the page view screen. Published pages are available at <code>/p/your-slug</code> or plain permalinks when configured. Use slug <code>welcome</code> or <code>home</code> as fallback homepage, or set the homepage under System → General → Reading.</p>
<p><strong>Inline media:</strong> Upload a featured/share image or block images directly on the page form (no need to visit Media first). New uploads appear in the Media library and get responsive sizes automatically.</p>
<p><strong>Duplicate:</strong> On the pages list and view screens, <strong>Duplicate</strong> creates a draft copy (title prefixed with “Copy of”), including visual layout (<code>layout_json</code>), blocks, SEO, parent, and password protection (the hash is copied — the clone stays locked). You are sent to the new draft’s editor. Needs <code>add_pages</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Bulk actions:</strong> On the pages list, select rows (or Select all on this page) and Apply: Publish, Set to draft, or Delete (max 100). Draft and delete skip the homepage and the fallback <code>welcome</code>/<code>home</code> pages. Needs <code>edit_pages</code> or <code>delete_pages</code>. Delete still needs a backup to restore.</p>
<p><strong>Password protect:</strong> Set a password on the page form (leave blank to keep the current one; check <strong>Remove password</strong> to make it public). Published URLs stay 200, but the body, layout, citation snippet, JSON body, and LLM listing are hidden until a visitor unlocks via the on-page form (CSRF, rate-limited). Logged-in editors with <code>edit_pages</code> skip the gate. Unlock is remembered in the session and a 10-day cookie; changing the password invalidates old unlocks. Protected pages are omitted from site search and <code>/llms.txt</code>. Playwright: <code>npm run test:e2e:cms-pulse-ux</code> (<code>BASE_URL</code>).</p>
<p><strong>Public preview:</strong> Unpublished pages stay 404 for visitors. Editors with <code>edit_pages</code> can open <code>?preview=1</code> (Preview on the view screen).</p>
<p><strong>SEO &amp; social:</strong> SEO title, meta description (150–160 chars), featured share image (1200×630 recommended), optional <code>noindex</code>, and <strong>content width</strong> override (full / wide / normal / narrow) for the public page layout. Site default content width is <strong>full</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>LLM / AI:</strong> Plain-language summary for AI crawlers; JSON export at <code>/p/{slug}.json</code> or <code>/index.json</code> for homepage; Schema.org JSON-LD on public HTML; listed in <code>/llms.txt</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Citation / BLUF:</strong> Citation snippet and FAQ pairs help AI search engines clip direct answers. Site defaults: System → General → AI search &amp; citation.</p>
<p>Site-wide: <code>/sitemap.xml</code>, <code>/robots.txt</code>, <code>/llms.txt</code>, <code>/llms-full.txt</code>, <code>/site.json</code>, <code>/blog.json</code>. Set <code>base_url</code> in config for absolute social URLs.</p>
<p><strong>While logged in:</strong> On the public site, editors and administrators see an edit bar on pages and posts with <strong>Edit via Frontend editor</strong> (visual builder) and <strong>Edit in admin</strong> (form). Visitors do not see these links.</p>
<p><strong>Sample layouts + menu:</strong> <code>npm run test:e2e:cms-pages-layouts-menu</code> publishes About / Services / Features / Team / Contact with different column layouts and adds them to the Primary Menu.</p>
<p><strong>Drag, width, and height demo:</strong> <code>npm run test:e2e:cms-builder-drag-column-size</code> opens a headed browser so you can watch Layers (including drag-reorder), Copy/Paste, reorder (⋮⋮ handle, modules into another column, ↑ ↓), the 1–12 width slider, dragging the edge between columns, and min height / vertical align (including Design on sections and rows). Uses <code>BASE_URL</code> from <code>.env.playwright</code> or <code>env.playwright</code> (example: <code>http://cms.local</code>).</p>
<p><strong>Team POGI demo site:</strong> <code>npm run test:e2e:cms-team-pogi-site</code> builds a branded site with 5 pages, 5 posts, free Lorem Picsum photos uploaded to Media, Primary Menu links, and Team POGI as the site name / homepage.</p>
